%% Hand-authored schematic; nine cfg outcomes verified by TLC on 2026-11-11.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Claimed: fresh claim (epoch, serial), same row
    Claimed --> Pending: stale pre-accept sweep; previous worker stays live
    Claimed --> Pending: clean cancellation; cancelled worker stops
    Claimed --> Accepted: fenced CAS; older worker may resume after same-token reclaim
    Accepted --> Spawned: CAS returns bool in Current/r2
    Spawned --> Scoped: Current private issue
    Spawned --> KeyReady: r2 old o_input creates private key
    KeyReady --> Scoped: key consumed by issuer scope, no proof return
    Scoped --> Entry: destructive first-entry take
    Entry --> Spent: normal drop before executor effects
    Spent --> Effects: normal execution
    Entry --> Recording: record attempt
    Recording --> Observed: by-value handoff, FS load
    Observed --> OwnerLock: DB begin
    Observed --> Observed: FS may change after observation (existing gap)
    Entry --> OwnerLock: pre-record rollback, proof moved
    OwnerLock --> RowLock: SELECT FOR UPDATE
    RowLock --> Commit: exact CAS
    Commit --> Pending: rollback or later exact release
    Pending --> Claimed: new serial; same process token may repeat
    Spawned --> StoredPermit: d1 CAS returns public receipt
    StoredPermit --> Unscoped: sibling retains receipt across executor entry
    Unscoped --> EffectsNoProof: executor effects without task-local proof
    EffectsNoProof --> LateProof: d1 public into_before_effects
    LateProof --> OwnerLock: return_before_record after effects
    Commit --> UnsafePending: d1 rollback commits after effects (RED)
    EffectsNoProof --> Rejected: Current/r2 have no convertible receipt/key
    Pending --> Restarted: process loss drops in-memory authority
    Restarted --> Claimed: new epoch and serial; no reconstruction
